{
  "analysis": "I'm starting fresh with a task about creating a mnemos workflow for project handoff. I can see several files in the workspace including session_notes.txt, memory_plan.json, and a skill_context directory. I need to explore these to understand the context and requirements.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace by reading the available files to understand the context. I'll start with session_notes.txt to see today's discussion, memory_plan.json for the memory structure, and check the skill_context directory for any relevant documentation.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat session_notes.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat memory_plan.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found the session_notes.txt which contains today's discussion about Project Northstar with facts about staged rollout, concise updates, weekly status summaries, and integration risk. The memory_plan.json already has a basic structure. Now I need to read the SKILL.md to understand the mnemos workflow requirements for storing memories, linking related facts, and creating recall summaries.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md file to understand the mnemos workflow requirements, then check the manifest.json for any additional context. After understanding the requirements, I'll implement the workflow to store facts, link related ones, and create a recall summary.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md output was truncated. I can see it describes the mnemon CLI tool for persistent memory - storing facts, recalling knowledge, linking related memories. I need to see the full workflow section to understand the commands. Let me read the full file and check if mnemon is installed.",
  "plan": "Read the full SKILL.md file using head/tail or less to see the complete workflow section, then check if mnemon is installed and available to use.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -100 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which mnemon\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md output is still truncated. I need to see the complete workflow section to understand the mnemon commands for remember, link, and recall. Let me read the entire file and check if mnemon is available.",
  "plan": "Read the complete SKILL.md file using cat with less or by reading it in chunks, and check if mnemon is installed.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | head -150\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mnemon --help 2>/dev/null || echo 'mnemon not found'\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md file content is being truncated. I need to read it differently to see the full workflow section. Let me try reading the file from line 100 onwards to see the workflow commands, and also check the setup.sh to understand how to set up the environment.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md file from line 100 onwards to see the workflow commands (remember, link, recall). Also check setup.sh and gen_inputs.py for any setup instructions.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '100,200p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Now I have the mnemon commands:\n- `mnemon remember \"<fact>\" --cat <cat> --imp <1-5> --entities \"e1,e2\" --source agent`\n- `mnemon link <id1> <id2> --type <type> --weight <0-1>`\n- `mnemon recall \"<query>\" --limit 10`\n\nCategories: preference, decision, insight, fact, context\nEdge types: temporal, semantic, causal, entity\n\nFrom session_notes.txt, I have these facts:\n1. Project Northstar uses a staged rollout\n2. Team preference: keep updates concise\n3. Decision: use weekly status summaries\n4. Insight: rollout risk is highest during integration\n\nI need to: store 3 facts, link related ones, recall for 'Northstar', categorize sensibly, use session as source.",
  "plan": "First run setup.sh to ensure environment is ready, then check if mnemon is installed. Then store the three facts with appropriate categories, link related facts (the rollout-related ones), and do a recall for 'Northstar'.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "bash setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mnemon --help 2>&1 || echo 'Need to install mnemon'\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Mnemon is not installed. I need to install it first. According to the SKILL.md, I can install via Homebrew or go install. Let me try go install since this appears to be a Linux environment.",
  "plan": "Install mnemon using go install, then verify it's working. After that, I'll store the facts, link related ones, and create the recall summary.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "go install github.com/mnemon-dev/mnemon@latest 2>&1\\n",
      "duration": 30
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Go is not installed. Let me check the gen_inputs.py script which might provide a way to set up the environment or simulate the mnemon workflow. I should also check if there are any pre-built binaries available.",
  "plan": "Read the gen_inputs.py to understand what it does, and check if there's an alternative way to install mnemon or if the script provides a mock/simulation of the workflow.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which python3 python curl wget\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Python3 is available. The gen_inputs.py just creates the input files. I need to find another way to install mnemon. Let me try using curl/wget to download a pre-built binary or install via apt.",
  "plan": "Try to install mnemon using apt-get or download a binary. Check what package managers are available.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get update && apt-get install -y wget curl 2>&1 | tail -5\\n",
      "duration": 30
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "curl and wget are now installed. Now I need to download and install the mnemon binary. Let me try to find a pre-built release or install via apt.",
  "plan": "Try to download mnemon from GitHub releases or install via apt. I'll check GitHub for releases first.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -L https://github.com/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases/latest/download/mnemon-linux-amd64.tar.gz -o /tmp/mnemon.tar.gz 2>&1 | tail -5\\n",
      "duration": 15
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The download only got 9 bytes - likely a redirect or wrong URL. Let me check what was downloaded and try an alternative approach - either install Go or find the correct binary URL.",
  "plan": "Check what was downloaded, then try to install Go to build mnemon, or find the correct binary download URL.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /tmp/mnemon.tar.gz\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get install -y golang-go 2>&1 | tail -10\\n",
      "duration": 60
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Go is being installed. Let me check if it's ready and then use it to install mnemon.",
  "plan": "Verify Go is installed, then use go install to get mnemon.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which go && go version\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "go install github.com/mnemon-dev/mnemon@latest 2>&1\\n",
      "duration": 60
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The go install is timing out due to network issues. Let me try downloading the mnemon binary directly from GitHub releases with a different approach, or check if there's a specific version available.",
  "plan": "Try to find and download the correct mnemon binary from GitHub releases. If that fails, I'll create a Python-based implementation that simulates the mnemon workflow for the task.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -sL https://api.github.com/repos/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases/latest | head -100\\n",
      "duration": 15
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found the GitHub releases API response. I can see there's a release v0.1.2 with assets. Let me get the full assets list to find the Linux binary URL.",
  "plan": "Extract the asset URLs from the GitHub API response to find the Linux amd64 binary, then download it.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -sL https://api.github.com/repos/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases/latest | grep -E '(browser_download_url|name)' | head -20\\n",
      "duration": 15
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Found the correct download URL for Linux amd64: https://github.com/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases/download/v0.1.2/mnemon_0.1.2_linux_amd64.tar.gz. Now I can download and install it.",
  "plan": "Download the mnemon binary from GitHub releases, extract it, and install it to /usr/local/bin.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -L https://github.com/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases/download/v0.1.2/mnemon_0.1.2_linux_amd64.tar.gz -o /tmp/mnemon.tar.gz\\n",
      "duration": 15
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tar -xzf /tmp/mnemon.tar.gz -C /tmp/ && ls -la /tmp/\\n",
      "duration": 1
    }
  ]
}
